.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH pvc-twarp 1  "pvc-twarp " 
.SH NAME
pvc\-twarp \- Time\-varying resynthesis: navigates a virtual time position through a `.pva` analysis file (rate/origin/window\-driven) and resynthesizes from whatever frame it lands on
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpvc\-twarp\fR [\fB\-\-duration\fR] [\fB\-\-window\-size\fR] [\fB\-\-window\fR] [\fB\-\-frames\-per\-sec\fR] [\fB\-\-time\-origin\fR] [\fB\-\-rate\fR] [\fB\-\-window\-low\fR] [\fB\-\-window\-high\fR] [\fB\-\-time\-response\fR] [\fB\-\-loop\-smooth\fR] [\fB\-\-window\-mode\fR] [\fB\-\-loop\-mode\fR] [\fB\-\-onset\-release\fR] [\fB\-\-pitch\fR] [\fB\-\-freq\-shift\fR] [\fB\-\-gain\fR] [\fB\-\-attack\fR] [\fB\-\-release\fR] [\fB\-\-freq\-response\-time\fR] [\fB\-\-warp\fR] [\fB\-\-shelf\-low\-gain\fR] [\fB\-\-shelf\-high\-gain\fR] [\fB\-\-shelf\-low\-freq\fR] [\fB\-\-shelf\-high\-freq\fR] [\fB\-\-threshold\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIANALYSIS\fR> <\fIOUTPUT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Time\-varying resynthesis: navigates a virtual time position through a `.pva` analysis file (rate/origin/window\-driven) and resynthesizes from whatever frame it lands on.
.PP
Ports `twarp`\*(Aqs audio\-processing path (`legacy/pvc_src/twarp.c`); see `pvc\-core::tools::twarp`\*(Aqs doc comment for what\*(Aqs in and out of scope (time\-point dither, loop\-boundary amplitude normalization, and random amplitude/frequency "shimmer" aren\*(Aqt ported yet).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-duration\fR \fI<DURATION>\fR [default: 0]
Output duration in seconds. `0` (the default) means "use the analysis file\*(Aqs own duration"
.TP
\fB\-\-window\-size\fR \fI<WINDOW_SIZE>\fR [default: 2048]
Analysis window length. `0` means auto (`2 * fft`, where `fft` is always the analysis file\*(Aqs own FFT size \- `twarp` has no independent `\-\-fft`). The C\*(Aqs own hardcoded default is a literal `2048`, matching `pv`\*(Aqs `\-\-window\-size` gotcha
.TP
\fB\-\-window\fR \fI<WINDOW>\fR [default: hamming]
Resynthesis window shape
.TP
\fB\-\-frames\-per\-sec\fR \fI<FRAMES_PER_SEC>\fR [default: 200]
Resynthesis frames per second (sets the hop size; there\*(Aqs no independent stretch factor \- unlike `pv`, `twarp`\*(Aqs hop always equals its own decimation)
.TP
\fB\-\-time\-origin\fR \fI<TIME_ORIGIN>\fR [default: 0]
Time\-position origin in seconds into the analysis data \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-rate\fR \fI<RATE>\fR [default: 1]
Playback rate multiplier (`1` = original speed, `2` = double speed, negative = reverse, `0` = stationary) \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-window\-low\fR \fI<WINDOW_LOW>\fR [default: 0]
Analysis time window low boundary in seconds \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-window\-high\fR \fI<WINDOW_HIGH>\fR [default: \-1]
Analysis time window high boundary in seconds (negative = end of analysis data) \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-time\-response\fR \fI<TIME_RESPONSE>\fR [default: 0]
Time\-position change response (smoothing) time in seconds \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-loop\-smooth\fR \fI<LOOP_SMOOTH>\fR [default: 0.2]
Sampler\-loop boundary smoothing time in seconds \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-window\-mode\fR \fI<WINDOW_MODE>\fR [default: loop]
Time\-window behavior: stop once time exits the window (`autostop`), or wrap/fold/clip at its edges forever (`loop`)
.TP
\fB\-\-loop\-mode\fR \fI<LOOP_MODE>\fR [default: wrap]
Sampler\-loop boundary behavior (only used in `loop` window mode)
.TP
\fB\-\-onset\-release\fR
Trigger the time window only once it\*(Aqs first entered, and extend the output duration on the way out to guarantee a full pass back to the window\*(Aqs edge (used for percussive onset + sustain\-loop + release shaping)
.TP
\fB\-\-pitch\fR \fI<PITCH>\fR [default: 0]
Pitch shift in semitones \- a plain number, or `@path`. Nonzero (or time\-varying) picks oscillator\-bank resynthesis; left at `0` (with `\-\-freq\-shift` also `0`) picks overlap\-add instead \- see `pvc\-core::tools::twarp`\*(Aqs doc comment
.TP
\fB\-\-freq\-shift\fR \fI<FREQ_SHIFT>\fR [default: 0]
Frequency shift in Hz \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-gain\fR \fI<GAIN>\fR [default: 0]
Gain in dB \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-attack\fR \fI<ATTACK>\fR [default: 0]
Amplitude envelope attack time in seconds \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-release\fR \fI<RELEASE>\fR [default: 0]
Amplitude envelope release time in seconds \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-freq\-response\-time\fR \fI<FREQ_RESPONSE_TIME>\fR [default: 0]
Frequency\-change response (smoothing) time in seconds \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-warp\fR \fI<WARP>\fR [default: 0]
Spectrum magnitude warp index (`0` = no warp) \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-shelf\-low\-gain\fR \fI<SHELF_LOW_GAIN>\fR [default: 0]
Low shelf EQ gain in dB \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-shelf\-high\-gain\fR \fI<SHELF_HIGH_GAIN>\fR [default: 0]
High shelf EQ gain in dB \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-shelf\-low\-freq\fR \fI<SHELF_LOW_FREQ>\fR [default: 200]
Low shelf EQ frequency in Hz \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-shelf\-high\-freq\fR \fI<SHELF_HIGH_FREQ>\fR [default: 2000]
High shelf EQ frequency in Hz \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-threshold\fR \fI<THRESHOLD>\fR [default: \-60]
Oscillator resynthesis threshold in dB
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIANALYSIS\fR>
Path to the `.pva` analysis file to resynthesize from
.TP
<\fIOUTPUT\fR>

